From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] vm: add native Promise state and direct async startup

Use GC-traced native Promise state behind explicit runtime activation,
preserving the existing public Promise surface after bootstrap. Keep
reaction ordering, thenable assimilation, rejection tracking, reentrant
collection, tracing configuration and bytecode/compiled callers aligned.

Aggregate guarded dense arrays of native Promises and primitives through
shared traced state and native reactions. Avoid per-element closures,
descriptors and discarded chained promises. Bound admission to 4096
elements and retain the JavaScript implementation for unsupported inputs
or observable method overrides.

Add optional compiler lowering for startup from a still-live async frame
and for private state machines with a reused completion record. Preserve
user-visible arguments, lexical environments, startup rejection and
exception cleanup; reject escaping factories and unsupported results.
Root the receiver, generator and private record across allocation.

Keep private bootstrap hooks, compiler options, runtime flags, trace
configuration and Promise/async semantic fixtures in the same patch.
